1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,668
KOMA is for comic fans: the people

2
00:00:02,668 --> 00:00:04,642
who make characters famous but never own

3
00:00:04,642 --> 00:00:07,208
them or get a say. Here, fans

4
00:00:07,208 --> 00:00:08,729
own the comic, and they write the

5
00:00:08,729 --> 00:00:09,599
canon.

6
00:00:10,267 --> 00:00:13,471
Sign-in is Privy: email, Google, a passkey,

7
00:00:13,471 --> 00:00:15,468
or a wallet you already have. We

8
00:00:15,468 --> 00:00:17,059
use a test wallet that holds no

9
00:00:17,059 --> 00:00:17,940
MON.

10
00:00:18,933 --> 00:00:22,299
The studio's editor is Tencent's Hunyuan 3.

11
00:00:22,660 --> 00:00:24,425
It turns a one-line idea into a

12
00:00:24,425 --> 00:00:26,979
pitch, with a title, style, pages and

13
00:00:26,979 --> 00:00:27,953
a price.

14
00:00:29,567 --> 00:00:33,816
Paying is HTTP 402. The server quotes

15
00:00:33,816 --> 00:00:36,625
a price, the wallet signs one AUSD

16
00:00:36,649 --> 00:00:39,807
authorization, and KOMA's facilitator settles it on

17
00:00:39,807 --> 00:00:42,720
Monad. No gas, no account.

18
00:00:43,367 --> 00:00:46,280
Executed in about four hundred fifty milliseconds,

19
00:00:46,304 --> 00:00:48,207
final in about nine hundred.

20
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:52,643
Kimi K2.6 writes the script, FLUX draws

21
00:00:52,643 --> 00:00:55,187
the panels, and the issue is minted

22
00:00:55,187 --> 00:00:56,427
to the buyer.

23
00:01:00,933 --> 00:01:02,872
The credits name the models that made

24
00:01:02,872 --> 00:01:04,579
it, and the reader has a guided

25
00:01:04,579 --> 00:01:06,981
mode that reads panel by panel.

26
00:01:17,599 --> 00:01:20,316
A series costs one dollar. FLUX draws

27
00:01:20,316 --> 00:01:22,429
a character sheet, and one transaction mints

28
00:01:22,429 --> 00:01:24,820
a character NFT with its own wallet,

29
00:01:24,820 --> 00:01:28,198
a coin and an AUSD bonding curve.

30
00:01:29,899 --> 00:01:32,717
Buying is a gasless signature. KOMA's relayer

31
00:01:32,717 --> 00:01:35,534
sends it with eth_sendRawTransactionSync, so the receipt

32
00:01:35,534 --> 00:01:38,351
comes back with the send: executed in

33
00:01:38,351 --> 00:01:41,168
two hundred thirteen milliseconds, final in under

34
00:01:41,168 --> 00:01:42,123
nine hundred.

35
00:01:45,233 --> 00:01:47,961
Holders propose the next episode. Kimi calls

36
00:01:47,961 --> 00:01:49,575
a tool to read the voted canon

37
00:01:49,575 --> 00:01:51,990
first, then writes it, drawn on model

38
00:01:51,990 --> 00:01:53,464
from the character sheet.

39
00:01:59,499 --> 00:02:01,717
Votes are free signatures, weighted by the

40
00:02:01,717 --> 00:02:04,596
coins held when the round opened. Three

41
00:02:04,596 --> 00:02:07,138
team wallets vote too; that's seeded, and

42
00:02:07,138 --> 00:02:08,240
we say so.

43
00:02:09,499 --> 00:02:11,775
While the vote runs, here is Monad

44
00:02:11,775 --> 00:02:14,886
testnet live: blocks moving from proposed to

45
00:02:14,886 --> 00:02:17,870
voted to finalized, the precompiles read on

46
00:02:17,870 --> 00:02:21,027
chain, and KOMA's own median confirmation.

47
00:02:24,733 --> 00:02:27,229
When the window closes, a Chainlink CRE

48
00:02:27,229 --> 00:02:30,550
workflow re-verifies every signature and weight, then

49
00:02:30,550 --> 00:02:32,453
settles the winner on Monad.

50
00:02:34,066 --> 00:02:36,365
Episode one is canon, and anyone who

51
00:02:36,365 --> 00:02:37,921
was away sees it the next time

52
00:02:37,921 --> 00:02:39,464
they open the series.

53
00:02:45,266 --> 00:02:48,317
The Writers' Room: one passkey derives keys

54
00:02:48,317 --> 00:02:51,369
that aren't a wallet. Drafts are encrypted

55
00:02:51,369 --> 00:02:54,420
in the browser, the server keeps only

56
00:02:54,420 --> 00:02:57,472
ciphertext, and each unlock is verified by

57
00:02:57,472 --> 00:02:58,930
Monad's P256 precompile.

58
00:03:09,099 --> 00:03:10,910
The shelf holds your issues and the

59
00:03:10,910 --> 00:03:13,209
characters you back, and every creator gets

60
00:03:13,209 --> 00:03:15,704
a page with what their characters earned.

61
00:03:21,665 --> 00:03:23,917
Signal Fire filled its curve tonight and

62
00:03:23,917 --> 00:03:27,132
graduated into a locked Uniswap v4 pool.

63
00:03:27,493 --> 00:03:29,595
Its story so far shows three canon

64
00:03:29,595 --> 00:03:33,193
episodes, each settled by Chainlink CRE.

65
00:03:36,365 --> 00:03:39,151
The board ranks series, backers and creators,

66
00:03:39,151 --> 00:03:41,137
and every payment step is explained in

67
00:03:41,137 --> 00:03:42,413
plain words.

68
00:03:53,965 --> 00:03:56,275
KOMA. Fans write the canon, live on

69
00:03:56,275 --> 00:03:57,598
Monad testnet.

